          "explanation": "Voltaire's 1759 novel Candide mocks Leibnizian optimism through Dr. Pangloss, whose insistence that all is for the best becomes absurd against a backdrop of real disasters modeled partly on the catastrophic 1755 Lisbon earthquake, which killed tens of thousands and forced Enlightenment thinkers to reckon with the problem of evil.",
